| **Ticket types (2024)** | 1. **Standard Guided Tour** – €12 (adult), €8 (senior/child 6‑12). <br>2. **Premium “Backstage” Tour** – €20 (includes orchestra‑pit access). <br>3. **Opera Performance Ticket** – €30 – €120 (depends on production and seat class). |
| **Languages** | Tours available in English, Italian, French, German, Spanish, and Russian (on request). |
| **Facilities** | • Wheelchair‑accessible routes (ramps & elevators). <br>• Audio‑guide devices (available for a €3 surcharge). <br>• Café “Caffè del Teatro” and a small gift shop selling music‑related souvenirs. |
| **Nearby points of interest** | • **Piazza Verdi** (the square surrounding the theatre). <br>• **Quattro Canti** (historic Baroque intersection, 5‑minute walk). <br>• **Mercato del Capo** (vibrant street market, 10‑minute walk). |
| **Best time to visit** | Early morning tours (10 am) avoid the midday crowds; the evening “Backstage” tour (starting at 5 pm) offers a quieter experience and a glimpse of the stage lights being set up. |

